<!--
    GH-873 (kuna): an AArch64 function returning a double in d0 prints as
    `undefined16 f(..)` with `v1._8_8_ = 0; return v1._0_16_;`.  The AArch64
    cspec's floating output entries are the 16-byte q0..q3, and SLEIGH lifts
    a scalar or 64-bit vector write (`fmov d0,#1.5`, `ldr d0,[x1]`,
    `movi d0,#0`, `add v0.2s,..`) as the low lane plus a COPY of zero into
    each higher lane of the register (zext_zd).  The zero reaches the RETURN
    as a second q0 trial, ancestorOpUse accepts a constant, and the output
    fill-in joins both halves.  The fill need not come from the instruction
    that wrote the returned value: `fmadd` has no fill in this SLEIGH spec.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "output-prototype".  The P0 assertion
    `option zerofillreturn on|off` decides whether a return trial above the
    low lane of a q register, whose value at every RETURN is the zero fill a
    narrow write left (marked on the p-code as lifted), is retired.

    Chunk 0x100000, clang 14 -O2 for aarch64-linux-gnu:
      double scale(int a, const double *g) { return *g * 1.5 + a; }
            (fmov d0,#1.5 fills; fmadd d0 writes the value without a fill)
      double zero(void) { return 0.0; }                     movi d0,#0
      double pick(double a, int k) { if (k) return a * 3; return a + 1; }
            (fcsel: the fill reaches the RETURN through a MULTIEQUAL)
      struct dd { double x, y; };
      struct dd pair(double a, int k) { struct dd r = { a * k, a + k }; return r; }
            (homogeneous aggregate in d0 and d1)
      int32x2_t add2(int32x2_t a, int32x2_t b) { return a + b; }  add v0.2s
            (control: a 64-bit vector built lane by lane, left as it was)
      int32x4_t comb(int32x2_t a, int32x2_t b)
            { return (int32x4_t){a[0] + b[0], a[1] + b[1], 0, 0}; }
            (control: the upper half is `mov v0.d[1],v2.d[0]` of a
            `movi v2.2d,#0`, a 128-bit value, not a fill)
    Chunk 0x101000, gcc 14.2 -O2 aarch64-linux-gnu, the same scale and zero
    (ldr d0,[x1] fills, then fmadd).
    Chunk 0x102000, hand assembled control `ins0`:
      movi v0.2d,#0; mov v0.d[0],x0; ret
            (a 128-bit zero write whose low lane is replaced: heritage splits
            it into the same two lanes, so it must keep its 16 bytes)

    Pass 1 (`option zerofillreturn off`) reproduces the BUG: scale, zero,
    pick and the gcc pair print `undefined16`, zero as `ZEXT816(0)`, pair
    returns q0 with an upper half of 0 instead of d1.
    Pass 2 (`option zerofillreturn on`, the shipped default) is the FIX:
    `double` returns, `return 0.0;`, pair joins d0 and d1; add2, comb and ins0
    print the same in both passes.
-->
